Do not release until languages/polski-pl_PL.po is imported into GlotPress.

Reason
------
1.29.8 stopped bundling .mo files, so every locale, Polish included, now comes
from the WordPress.org language pack. That pack is built from
translate.wordpress.org.

1.30.0 replaced about 520 Polish source strings with English ones, so every
msgid on translate.wordpress.org for those strings is stale. Until the new
pl_PL catalogue is imported there, the pack cannot match them.

Releasing before the import leaves Polish shops with an English interface,
including the statutory withdrawal instructions and the model withdrawal form.

How to clear this
-----------------
1. Import polski/polski/languages/polski-pl_PL.po into the wp-plugins/polski
   dev/pl/default/ and stable/pl/default/ sub-projects on
   translate.wordpress.org. This needs PTE, so it cannot be done from a script.

2. Confirm the pl_PL pack rebuilt:

     curl -s "https://api.wordpress.org/translations/plugins/1.0/?slug=polski" \
       | python3 -c "import sys,json;[print(t['language'],t['version'],t['updated']) for t in json.load(sys.stdin)['translations']]"

   pl_PL should report the version being released, or one close to it, with a
   fresh timestamp.

3. Delete this file, commit the deletion, then run the release.

Worth importing at the same time: languages/polski-es_ES.po. Spanish has no
pack at all today, so the Spanish interface falls back to English. It is
AI-assisted, so a GTE may refuse it; see plogins-plugins/GLOTPRESS-IMPORT.md.

Raised 2026-08-27 with the 1.30.0 source-string change.
